cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VulnGen: A Reproducible Framework for Assessing Security in LLM-Generated Code"
message: "If you use this framework, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tiwari
    given-names: Anuansh
    affiliation: "Amity University, Lucknow, India"
abstract: >-
  VulnGen is a defensive framework for evaluating security-relevant defects in
  code using a SAST ensemble with manual adjudication, together with a study
  harness that produces measured, traceable results on public datasets.
repository-code: "https://github.com/glassgotlazy/vulngen"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - software security
  - static analysis
  - large language models
  - CWE
  - reproducibility
